Front-End Website Audit Report

1. Website Strengths

1. Clean and Simple Design
   The website has a clean and simple design. The layout is easy to understand and does not
   feel unnecessarily complicated.

1. Easy Navigation
   The navigation is smooth and easy to use. The main sections, such as Courses, Services,
   About, and Contact, are clearly separated, making it easy for users to move around the
   website.

1. Simple and Modern Color Combination
   The website uses a simple and modern color combination. The colors work well together
   and give the website a professional appearance.

1. Responsive Design
   The website works well on different screen sizes. The layout adjusts properly for both
   smaller and larger screens, which provides a better experience for different devices.

1. Smooth User Experience
   The website feels smooth while browsing. Pages and sections are easy to access, and there
   were no major usability problems noticed during the audit

1. Improvement Opportunities

1. HTTPS / Security Certificate Warning
   A security certificate warning appeared when accessing the website. This should be
   checked and fixed because users may feel unsafe when a browser displays a security
   warning.

1. Dark Mode / Night Mode Option
   The website could include a Dark Mode toggle button. The bright interface can feel
   uncomfortable to view in low-light conditions, especially at night. A Dark Mode option
   could make the website more comfortable and improve the user experience.

1. Correct Social Media Link
   The Facebook icon should link directly to the company’s official Facebook page. Currently,
   clicking the Facebook icon redirects to the website instead of opening the Facebook page.
   The link should be checked and connected to the correct social media page.

Front-End Best Practices Summary

A good website should follow these front-end best practices:

1. Clean and Simple UI – Keep the interface clean, simple, and easy to understand.
2. Easy Navigation – Navigation should be clear, consistent, and easy for users to use.
3. Responsive Design – The website should work properly on mobile, tablet, and desktop
   screens.
4. Consistent Colors and Typography – Use consistent colors and readable fonts
   throughout the website.
5. Good User Experience – The website should provide a smooth and comfortable
   experience for users.
6. Fast Performance – Optimize images, CSS, and JavaScript to improve loading speed.
7. Accessibility – Use readable text, proper labels, good contrast, and keyboard-friendly
   navigation.
8. Clear Content Structure – Organize content using clear headings and sections.
9. Functional Links and Buttons – All buttons, navigation links, and social media links
   should work correctly.
10. Security and Trust – Use a valid HTTPS/SSL certificate to avoid browser security
    warnings.

Conclusion

Good front-end development focuses on simplicity, usability, responsiveness,
performance, accessibility, security, and a smooth user experience
